From 73a6648a2d2d92d9b5842d2881a259a626e1df52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Certe Kim <18364439+CerteKim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:45:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x: describe the remaining apps_smmu
 context interrupts

The vendor IORT (matching the firmware's own devicetree, which lists the first
106 of them) describes 128 context interrupts for the APPS SMMU, in the same
order as the 106 already in sc8180x.dtsi. In EL1 QHEE emulates the SMMU and
reports 106 context banks, so the truncated list is enough there; with Secure
Launch (slbounce) the real hardware reports 127 context banks in IDR1 and
arm_smmu_device_probe() rejects the devicetree with "found only 106 context
irq(s) but 127 required".

Append the missing 21 entries (GSIV 0x308..0x31c) so the same devicetree works
in both cases: arm-smmu truncates the list to num_context_banks, so EL1 is
unaffected. This also lets the EL2 overlay drop its padded (invented) copy of
the property, which registered context fault handlers on SPIs that belong to no
context bank.

The 128th entry of the IORT (0x31d) is deliberately not added: the hardware
only has 127 context banks.
